content.text:
In light mode, the white background visible in the demo player is coming from **two places** in the demo runner and component hierarchy:

1. **The demo runner's result iframe background:**
   - In [tools/demo/runner/runner.css](tools/demo/runner/runner.css#L41) and [tools/demo/runner/runner.css](tools/demo/runner/runner.css#L170), the runner specifies:
     ```css
     body {
       background: var(--instui-color-background-base, Canvas);
     }
     .runner__result {
       background: var(--instui-color-background-base, #fff);
     }
     ```
   - In light mode (`rebrand`), `--instui-color-background-base` resolves to `#ffffff` (white), whereas `--instui-color-background-page` is `#f2f4f5` (light grey).

2. **The reset rule in `base.css`:**
   - In [formats/components/src/rules/base/base.css](formats/components/src/rules/base/base.css#L21-L23):
     ```css
     :where(html) {
       background: var(--instui-color-background-page);
     }
     :where(body) {
       margin: 0;
     }
     ```
   - Because `base.css` sets `background: var(--instui-color-background-page)` on `:where(html)` while `:where(body)` has no explicit background, standard iframe rendering rules cause the transparent `<body>` and `<html>` to reveal the parent `.runner__result` / `.runner body` container background (`--instui-color-background-base` = white).

### How to resolve

- **If the demo should have a page background:** 
  Add `background: var(--instui-color-background-page);` to [docs/demos/pendo/style.css](docs/demos/pendo/style.css) (or in [tools/demo/runner/runner.css](tools/demo/runner/runner.css#L170) on `.runner__result`) so it explicitly paints the page background color instead of inheriting/showing `background-base`.
